{"request_id": "34e3579d-9a61-4ec7-b29c-29a061161d15", "run_id": "a6bbe7f6-7c77-449a-ab5c-5494e09f2269", "scenario": "real_calibration", "source": "real", "start_time": "2026-11-10T21:19:28.840640+00:00", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "question_id": "attention", "retrieval_setting": "small", "max_completion_tokens": 768, "reasoning_effort": "low", "status": "ok", "http_status": 200, "first_event_ms": 919.31, "first_token_ms": 919.43, "last_content_ms": 983.19, "total_ms": 983.85, "tokens_in": 601, "tokens_out": 124, "reasoning_tokens": 5, "finish_reason": "stop", "piece_count": 110, "retries": 0, "headers": {"x-ratelimit-limit-requests": "1000", "x-ratelimit-limit-tokens": "8000", "x-ratelimit-remaining-requests": "996", "x-ratelimit-remaining-tokens": "6841", "x-ratelimit-reset-requests": "5m45.6s", "x-ratelimit-reset-tokens": "8.692s"}, "answer": "Scaled dot\u2011product attention is computed by taking the dot product of each query with all keys, dividing each result by \\(\\sqrt{d_k}\\), applying a softmax to obtain attention weights, and then weighting the values by these weights:  \n\n\\[\n\\text{Attention}(Q,K,V)=\\operatorname{softmax}\\!\\left(\\frac{QK^{\\top}}{\\sqrt{d_k}}\\right)V \\quad\\text{[1706.03762v7, PDF p. 4]} .\n\\]", "error": null}
{"request_id": "f05c7c86-4439-4040-b65f-5d5033077643", "run_id": "a6bbe7f6-7c77-449a-ab5c-5494e09f2269", "scenario": "real_calibration", "source": "real", "start_time": "2026-11-10T21:19:41.827817+00:00", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "question_id": "moshi", "retrieval_setting": "small", "max_completion_tokens": 768, "reasoning_effort": "low", "status": "ok", "http_status": 200, "first_event_ms": 413.58, "first_token_ms": 413.83, "last_content_ms": 470.89, "total_ms": 472.75, "tokens_in": 468, "tokens_out": 101, "reasoning_tokens": 4, "finish_reason": "stop", "piece_count": 88, "retries": 0, "headers": {"x-ratelimit-limit-requests": "1000", "x-ratelimit-limit-tokens": "8000", "x-ratelimit-remaining-requests": "995", "x-ratelimit-remaining-tokens": "7408", "x-ratelimit-reset-requests": "7m12s", "x-ratelimit-reset-tokens": "4.439s"}, "answer": "Moshi achieves full\u2011duplex spoken dialogue by modelling two streams\u2014semantic tokens and acoustic tokens\u2014hierarchically within a single multi\u2011stream speech\u2011to\u2011speech Transformer. This architecture allows the model to consume the user\u2019s linguistic and non\u2011linguistic (acoustic) input while simultaneously generating speech in real time, enabling simultaneous two\u2011way conversation. [2410.00037v1, PDF p. 6]", "error": null}
{"request_id": "ad7a613d-0f35-4afe-baef-cad673ac624f", "run_id": "a6bbe7f6-7c77-449a-ab5c-5494e09f2269", "scenario": "real_calibration", "source": "real", "start_time": "2026-11-10T21:19:54.303170+00:00", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "question_id": "hnet", "retrieval_setting": "small", "max_completion_tokens": 1024, "reasoning_effort": "low", "status": "ok", "http_status": 200, "first_event_ms": 819.43, "first_token_ms": 884.57, "last_content_ms": 966.53, "total_ms": 996.05, "tokens_in": 669, "tokens_out": 169, "reasoning_tokens": 36, "finish_reason": "stop", "piece_count": 124, "retries": 0, "headers": {"x-ratelimit-limit-requests": "1000", "x-ratelimit-limit-tokens": "8000", "x-ratelimit-remaining-requests": "994", "x-ratelimit-remaining-tokens": "6819", "x-ratelimit-reset-requests": "8m38.4s", "x-ratelimit-reset-tokens": "8.857s"}, "answer": "- H\u2011Net learns chunking boundaries **end\u2011to\u2011end**, letting the model discover semantically meaningful units automatically.  \n- The dynamic approach lets the network **compress low\u2011information regions** while keeping high\u2011information content at an appropriate granularity.  \n- The **chunking layer** (named *Chunk* in equation\u202f(2)) contains a **routing module** that decides where to split the sequence.  \n- A **downsampler** follows the routing module to reduce the sequence length according to the chosen boundaries.  \n\n[2507.07955v2, PDF p.\u202f6]", "error": null}
